This is a basic kernel module that prints the string "Hello World".
The module can receive params to print the string "Hello World" n times.

Compile & test
-----------------------

After clone:
1. make

2. sudo insmod helloworld.ko repeat=4

3. "dmesg | tail" should display "Hello world n: n" n times according to the param
passed.

Remove:

4. sudo rmmod helloworld

5. "dmesg | tail" to see the exit message.

6. "sudo rmmod helloworld" to remove the module from your kernel.

If no params are passed the module will use the default value: 1.
